itches `round_money` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, e.g. `2.665 -> 2.66`, `2.675 -> 2.68`.\n\nCI: run ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fin-212-bankers-rounding", "confidence": 0.93}, "confidence": 0.93}, {"t_ms": 419625, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_014XHQDS1s3wzphmoEd5CY5y", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["reconcile_lookup", "reconciled_executed", "postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fin-212-bankers-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 419625, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_014XHQDS1s3wzphmoEd5CY5y", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 422474, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_019J2sYq67KwJPpbnq4ZBV4L", "tool": "request_review", "args": {"number": 101, "reviewers": ["alex"], "confidence": 0.9}, "confidence": 0.9}, {"t_ms": 422774, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_019J2sYq67KwJPpbnq4ZBV4L", "tool": "request_review", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 422774, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_019J2sYq67KwJPpbnq4ZBV4L", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 428330, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and PR #101 is open against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own docstring says it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, per FIN-212). That made the `test_half_even` test fail: `2.665` rounded to `2.67` instead of `2.66`.\n- **Fix:** On a new branch, `fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding`, I changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. That's the only change.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** #101 (https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101). When the PR was created it came back with no reviewers, so I added alex separately and he's now listed.\n\nThe PR still needs a code owner's approval before it can be merged; I haven't merged it. I also tried to look up FIN-212 in the advisory tool, but it isn't there, so this fix relies only on the test and the docstring.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01PywGzAXrJRrq9qkRfehndh", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_014J5MsjzWY549pXWUR7mxNT", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_015ohRSgfhnCbsLnnhqLYt6d", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212", "confidence": 0.7}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01M49EhQLZwyXgobvu8XmcYx", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "from_ref": "main", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_011QVCYMjHUMD6NWiXowTKjG", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "message": "Use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) in round_money per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), roun